      <activity id="04a496a2-1de0-5fdc-9dc3-7614e1e22a75" activityNameId="ea8b1d17-10ae-5763-8a0d-e6de835edc38" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Crude oil, at production</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Crude oil, at production
Oil production delivers the co-product natural gas. The values are derived from a multioutput-process "combined onshore gas and oil production" by allocation based on heating values for crude oil and natural gas UUID=678aec51-f80c-3d21-b062-a6124b755d48
Production of crude oil including energy use, infrastructure and emissions.
Location: Data valid for AZ.
Technology: 90 % offshore and  10 % onshore production
Time period: Time of most relevant publications and statistics. Other generic data, e.g. for infrastructure are based on older publications.
Production volume: 30 megatons of crude oil per year in 2023.
Sampling: Statistics and use of generic data
Extrapolations: A part of the data has been estimated with generic assumptions for on- and offshore production.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_678aec51-f80c-3d21-b062-a6124b755d48.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
